cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PySNT in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "PySNT: Python interface for SNT"
abstract: >-
  PySNT is a Python interface for SNT, the open-source framework for
  quantification of neuronal anatomy. It runs SNT in-process, so
  reconstructions, measurements and images move directly between SNT and the
  scientific Python stack (e.g., NumPy, SciPy, scikit-learn, NetworkX,
  napari), without a separate Fiji workflow. It ships with Computational
  Neuroanatomy: A Hands-on Curriculum in Python.
authors:
